Provenance and license map for sys/dev/drm/nouveau
==================================================

This directory implements nvkm, the DragonFly-native NVIDIA GSP driver.
It exposes the Linux nouveau userspace ABI (Mesa/NVK sees a standard
nouveau device) but it is not a port of the GPL nouveau driver.  Two
kinds of code live here, and the boundary matters for licensing and
review.

1. DragonFly-native code (SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause)

   Every nvkm_*.c and nvkm_*.h file at the top of this directory, plus
   nouveau_bo.h (a small DragonFly-local shim, despite the name) and
   nvkm.c.  These are original implementations.  Where they follow the
   algorithms or object-model semantics of Linux nouveau, they were
   rewritten natively from the algorithm, never copied from GPL text;
   comments cite the reference (for example "matches nouveau
   tu102_gsp_fini") as attribution, not as provenance.

   The DragonFly bridge that drives the imported display classes lives
   here as well (nvkm_dispnv50_bridge.c), so the import directories
   below contain only imported files.

2. Imported MIT code from the Linux kernel nouveau tree

   Imported files keep their upstream MIT license text and their
   upstream layout so they stay directly diffable against the source
   tree.  The import baseline is the Linux v7.0 nouveau tree
   (drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau); interface definitions were cross-checked
   against NVIDIA open-gpu-kernel-modules tag 570.144 (MIT), the exact
   match for the GSP-RM 570.144 firmware this driver boots.

   Directory map (local path  <-  upstream path):

   core/*.c        <-  nvkm/core/*.c
   core/*.h        <-  include/nvkm/core/*.h
   engine/disp.h   <-  include/nvkm/engine/disp.h
   engine/disp/    <-  nvkm/engine/disp/
   dispnv50/       <-  dispnv50/             EVO core/window/head/
                                             cursor/wimm/sor classes
   nvhw/           <-  include/nvhw/         hardware definition headers
   nvif/           <-  include/nvif/         nouveau interface classes
   nvrm/           <-  include/nvrm/         GSP-RM base types
   rm/             <-  nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/   RM API and handle
                                             definitions
   subdev/         <-  include/nvkm/subdev/  subdev interface headers

   Upstream's include/ headers are flattened next to their consumers,
   which keeps the upstream spelling of #include <nvif/...>,
   <nvhw/...>, <nvrm/...>, <core/...>, <engine/...>, and <subdev/...>
   lines intact.

   Modification policy for imported files: keep the upstream text
   intact.  DragonFly adaptations are compile-gated with
   NVKM_DFLY_GSP_DISPLAY_ONLY so a diff against the upstream file
   shows exactly what changed and why; this tree builds only for
   DragonFly, so no __DragonFly__ preprocessor conditionals are used.
   Several files are still byte-identical to upstream, for
   example core/object.c, core/object.h, core/enum.c, nvhw/drf.h,
   nvif/class.h, and nvrm/nvtypes.h.

3. Firmware (fw/)

   NVIDIA GSP-RM 570.144 boot blobs, packaged from linux-firmware
   under the linux-firmware NVIDIA firmware license.  Image names keep
   the linux-firmware paths (nvidia/tu102/...).  The larger blobs are
   extracted at build time from the local /lib/firmware install; see
   fw/Makefile.

Rules
-----

   - MIT/BSD-licensed headers and files may be copied verbatim.
   - GPL logic is never copied; it may only be reimplemented natively
     from the algorithm.
   - No file in this tree may carry MODULE_LICENSE("GPL"),
     EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL, or GPL-only license text.

   tools/tools/drm/nouveau/kms_static_audit.py scans the display/KMS
   file set and the evidence tools for these invariants and records
   the result in /var/tmp/nvkm-kms-static-audit.json.
